<title>SOUTH AFRICA: Avgold waits firmer gold before more hedges.</title>
<headline>Avgold waits firmer gold before more hedges.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1997-07-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>South African gold mining company Avgold Ltd said on Tuesday that it would not hedge further production until the bullion price rose.</p>
<p>&quot;We're waiting for the gold price to firm before we hedge more gold,&quot; said David Kovarsky, investment relations manager.</p>
<p>He said that the company's current hedging programme had won for it an average gold price for the second quarter that was 2,900 rand/kg higher than the spot price.</p>
<p>Avgold's average revenue for the quarter was 52,325 rand/kg.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom +27 11 482-1003</p>
</text>
